															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lichruler" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5953422); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5953422&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607526662" alt="Lichruler" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5953422)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lichruler" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5953422); return false;" >Lichruler</a></span> <span class="odate time_1576615341 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">17 Dec 2019 20:42</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4448814">
									

<p>SO I'm a bit of a Fallout fan, and I recently realized in the various games I have played in the franchise, that there was never an organization or group that was dedicated about the various horrible creatures in Fallout, even before the great war.</p>
<p>In Fallout, we know there were people experimenting with the Forced Evolution Virus, which made super mutants and other horrid creatures. We know that people were aware of the Zetans, the alien race that has been antagonizing and messing with humans for literally hundreds of years. There was also the various lovecraftian-style cults about worshiping various extra-dimensional monsters (which may actually exist).</p>
<p>With all of these various creatures, even before the bombs dropped, you'd think there would be some form of organization to try and contain these various things before they became a problem. After the bombs fell, that's another story, but surely there had to be something, if not in America, then maybe somewhere else.</p>
<p>Thoughts?</p>

